Requirements
Use Jetpack Compose Canvas, Android Bitmap/Canvas for snapshots, Kotlin standard library, and JDK concurrency primitives only. Do not use Android View, TextureView, SurfaceView, RenderThread, coroutines, RxJava, or third-party rendering libraries.
The constructor must throw IllegalArgumentException if maxCachedTiles <= 0. Public methods may be called from any thread. Tile commits and Compose-observed state mutations must happen on the main thread.
Tiles are fixed 256 x 256 screen pixels. Tile (0, 0) covers [0, 256) x [0, 256). Tile (1, 0) covers [256, 512) x [0, 256). Negative tile coordinates are allowed for prefetching.
The viewport transform is:
screenX = (sceneX - offsetX) * scale
screenY = (sceneY - offsetY) * scale
setViewport requires finite scale > 0 and finite offsets. Invalid values throw IllegalArgumentException.
A viewport change invalidates all pending and committed tiles. Old raster results from previous viewport generations must not commit.
beginStroke requires non-empty strokeId and finite widthPx > 0; otherwise throw IllegalArgumentException. Duplicate active stroke IDs are rejected. Strokes render in begin order.
Each stroke has a monotonically increasing revision. The first begin for an ID creates revision 0; reusing a previously removed ID creates a revision greater than any previous revision for that ID. appendPoints, endStroke, removeStroke, and restyleStroke advance the affected stroke’s revision or tombstone revision.
appendPoints requires all coordinates and pressures to be finite, and pressures to be >= 0. It copies the input list before returning. Empty lists are no-ops after validation. Calling appendPoints on an ended or missing stroke throws IllegalArgumentException.
Stroke geometry is deterministic. A single-point stroke draws a round dot. Multiple-point strokes connect adjacent points with round-capped, round-joined line segments. Segment width is stroke.widthPx * average(pointA.pressure, pointB.pressure). A segment with width 0 draws nothing.
endStroke marks a stroke as no longer appendable. removeStroke removes an active stroke; removing a missing stroke is a no-op. restyleStroke changes color and width; missing strokes are no-ops.
Normal stroke mutations must use dirty-only invalidation. Appending, ending, removing, or restyling a stroke invalidates only tiles intersecting the affected old/new stroke bounds, expanded by the relevant stroke radius. Do not clear all pending or committed tiles unless the dirty bounds cover all such tiles.
Unaffected committed tiles must remain reusable after stroke edits. Unaffected pending jobs may still commit if their captured viewport/cache generations and captured stroke revisions are still current.
Raster jobs use immutable snapshots of viewport, tile key, active strokes intersecting that tile, captured stroke revisions, viewport generation, and cache generation. A tile result may commit only if the tile is still pending for that exact job and all captured stroke revisions are still current.
undo reverts the most recent mutation among begin, append, end, remove, and restyle. redo reapplies the most recently undone mutation. Undo/redo must use dirty-only invalidation for affected stroke bounds. A new stroke mutation after undo clears the redo stack.
clear removes all strokes, clears undo/redo history, clears pending and committed tiles, and rejects old raster results.
The composable must not block waiting for raster jobs. When composed at a positive pixel size, it schedules missing visible tiles before prefetch tiles. Prefetch tiles are the one-tile ring around the visible tile rectangle.
Scheduling must be driven only by ConcurrentStrokeCanvas being composed at a positive pixel size. Tests must not call private/internal scheduling helpers. Recomposition, redraw, size changes, or state revision changes may trigger scheduling, but duplicate pending jobs for the same tile and current generation are forbidden.
Committed tiles represent the raster cache. In-progress strokes whose latest revision is not represented in a committed visible tile must be drawn as a live vector overlay above committed tiles. The overlay must use the same stroke geometry and must not mutate committed bitmaps.
Missing visible tiles draw the white background, plus any required live overlay. Committed visible tiles draw in row-major order: top-to-bottom, then left-to-right.
The tile cache is LRU-capped by maxCachedTiles. Evict least-recently-used non-visible tiles first. Tiles visible in the current draw must not be evicted during that draw, even if the cache temporarily exceeds the cap. Reading a committed tile during composable drawing or renderSnapshot makes it recently used.
renderSnapshot(width, height) requires positive dimensions. It renders into a new Bitmap using one immutable snapshot. It must not call a composable, schedule raster jobs, wait for workers, or commit results. It must use the same rendering rules as the composable, including live overlay.
debugState() returns a stable snapshot without mutating state, scheduling jobs, waiting for workers, or exposing mutable internal collections. commitThreadIds records the thread id used for each committed tile since construction or latest clear; every value must equal mainThreadId.
submittedTileKeys records tile submission order since construction or latest clear. rejectedCommitCount counts stale tile results rejected at commit time. evictedTiles records tile eviction order since construction or latest clear.
The implementation must not deadlock under concurrent viewport changes, stroke mutations, undo/redo, clear, composition/drawing, snapshots, and out-of-order worker completions.



